select '2026-08-02.1', 'PARA-0002', 'JAPAN_TRAVEL_001', 'A Family Trip to Japan', 'Travel / Culture', 'B1–B2', 'Last summer, my family travelled to Japan for visit several cities. We stayed in a hotel which was located near from the railway station, so travelling was very convenience. On the first day, we collected many informations from a tourist centre and asked the staff where should we go. They suggested us to visit an ancient temple that built over five hundred years ago. Although the weather was heavily raining, the temple was more beautiful than I expected. If we had brought an umbrella, we would not got wet. Overall, the journey gave us many memory and broaden our knowledge.', 'Last summer, my family travelled to Japan to visit several cities. We stayed in a hotel which was located near the railway station, so travelling was very convenient. On the first day, we collected much information from a tourist centre and asked the staff where we should go. They suggested that we visit an ancient temple that was built over five hundred years ago. Although it was raining heavily, the temple was more beautiful than I expected. If we had brought an umbrella, we would not have got wet. Overall, the journey gave us many memories and broadened our knowledge.', 100, 100, 7, 12, 'British English', 'Edmund Sir', 'approved', 1, true, false, 'Travel vocabulary with infinitive, preposition, countability, indirect-question, passive and conditional errors.'
