select '2026-08-02.1', 'PARA-0010', 'SCHOOL_UNIFORMS_EQUALITY_AND_PRACTICAL_COSTS_0010', 'School Uniforms, Equality and Practical Costs', 'Education / School Policy / Student Well-being', 'B1–B2', 'In many schools, In order to train students discipline. Schools have stringent requestment in uniform. Some schools allow children to dress with for more freedom. Requiring pupils to wear a uniform has several clear benefits, especially wearing uniform can help students more focus on studies, but schools allowing casual wear will increase the time and cost and even cause psychological problems. One major advantage Wearing uniform can reduce this wearing anxiety and help students concentrate on studies. If students spend less time choosing outfits clothes, they can reserve more time for homework and get quality time to sleep in the morning, as well as students maintain energy in the lesson. Uniforms can create the fair schools environment. If schools allow the students causal wear, everyday schools will become a faishon show, Some affluent student dressed to flex, while a normal students only have 2-3 outfits to change. Teenagers value their friendships and care about what their think, personal outfits become a main topic in schools. If some students can''t expand that even cause bullying in school. Therefore children will face mental health problems. For these reasons uniforms can reslove the students choosing outfits problems and make campus life equal. However schools uniforms also have disadvantages. the most obvious one is that uniforms are not comfortable and practical. Although uniforms look decent, they can''t take away sweat and uniform quality not warm in the winnter. For example the student finishing the PE leasson T-shirt always get wet and the jacket too thin can''t keep warm. Another drawback is cost. Although uniforms are meant to simplify clothing but the suppliers price increase every years. If the students in developmental stage, keep to change every year. For income family this become a heavy hidden financial burden. Therefore uniforms may solve social problems at schools, but they can also create parents and students economic difficulties. In conclusion school uniforms can make wearing easier for the students and reduce comparison but they can cause financial pressure. Overall, they bring clear learning environment benefits, while also creating practical and personal drawbacks.', 'In many schools, uniforms are required in order to instil discipline in students. Schools have stringent uniform requirements. Some schools allow children to dress more freely. Requiring pupils to wear a uniform has several clear benefits, especially because wearing a uniform can help students focus more on studies, but schools allowing casual wear will increase the time and cost and even cause psychological problems. One major advantage is that wearing a uniform can reduce anxiety about clothing and help students concentrate on studies. If students spend less time choosing outfits, they can reserve more time for homework, have more time to sleep in the morning, and maintain energy in the lesson. Uniforms can create a fair school environment. If schools allow the students to wear casual clothes, schools will become fashion shows every day; some affluent students dress to flex, while normal students have only 2-3 outfits to change into. Teenagers value their friendships and care about what their friends think, so personal outfits become a main topic in schools. If some students can''t afford such clothes, this may even cause bullying in school. Therefore, children will face mental health problems. For these reasons, uniforms can resolve students'' problems with choosing outfits and make campus life equal. However, school uniforms also have disadvantages. The most obvious one is that uniforms are neither comfortable nor practical. Although uniforms look decent, they can''t wick away sweat and they are not warm in winter. For example, after a student finishes a PE lesson, their T-shirt always gets wet, and their jacket is too thin to keep them warm. Another drawback is cost. Although uniforms are meant to simplify clothing, the suppliers'' prices increase every year. If the students are at a developmental stage, they need to change their uniforms every year. For low-income families, this becomes a heavy hidden financial burden. Therefore, uniforms may solve social problems at schools, but they can also create economic difficulties for parents and students. In conclusion, school uniforms can make dressing easier for the students and reduce comparison, but they can cause financial pressure. Overall, they bring clear learning environment benefits, while also creating practical and personal drawbacks.', 345, 361, 23, 51, 'British English', 'Edmund Sir', 'approved', 1, false, false, 'Dataset 10 from the supplied Grammar Dataset 3 to 18 PDF. Approved for canonical storage in the development partition; excluded from live retrieval pending a separate production review.'
