select '2026-08-02.1', 'PARA-0011', 'WORKING_HOURS_AND_PERSONAL_BOUNDARIES_0011', 'Working Hours and Personal Boundaries', 'Employment / Work–life Balance / Government Policy', 'B1–B2', 'In today''s society, work become a part of our life, so our private time it has been connected with our work. This problem is usually caused by over workload leads to work stress and weakened boundaries between professional and private life. If the government set a limits maximum working hour and set personal boundaries can protect employees work life balance. One major reason is that many employess facing a heavy workload. Nowadays messaging app are common caused staff have a lot of email messages to reply, since it is so convenient to manage documents and meetings, so the end of the working day no longer feels like a real end. As a result a person may be physically at home, but mentally still at the office desk. Another cause is financial pressure. Face of high house prices, bus fares and food keep going up, people give up their free time and face heavy work stress just to keep their jobs. Over time, their tired bodies to make money. Because they do not have enough rest for a long time, they work become slower and slower and need more time to finish the work, After that, they lose their personal life. The most effective solution is the government to limit the maximum working hours for certain jobs. For examples, clerks and sales assistants can only work 6 days per week and 8 hours per day. Also the employees can choose not to read or reply the work messages after work, and theirs bosses cannot punish or give them bad reviews for this. Hope this can help workers keep more personal and more rest time. At the same time people should set a clear boundaries for work. For examples, after work turn off work notifications, and leaves more time for doing exercise and having family dinners. Without such boundaries, personal life becomes the first thing to be sacrificed. In conclusion, work stress and financial pressure is closely connected to our standard of living and quality of life. However If the government and employers give a better work condition and individuals draw a clearer line between their jobs and the rests of their lives.this problem can be solved.', 'In today''s society, work has become a part of our lives, so our private time has been connected with our work. This problem is usually caused by excessive workloads, which lead to work stress and weakened boundaries between professional and private life. If the government sets a maximum limit on working hours and employees set personal boundaries, these measures can protect employees'' work-life balance. One major reason is that many employees face a heavy workload. Nowadays, messaging apps are common, causing staff to have a lot of email messages to reply to; since it is so convenient to manage documents and meetings, the end of the working day no longer feels like a real end. As a result, a person may be physically at home, but mentally still at the office desk. Another cause is financial pressure. Faced with high house prices, rising bus fares and food prices, people give up their free time and face heavy work stress just to keep their jobs. Over time, their bodies become tired as they work to make money. Because they do not have enough rest for a long time, they work more and more slowly and need more time to finish the work; after that, they lose their personal life. The most effective solution is for the government to limit the maximum working hours for certain jobs. For example, clerks and sales assistants can only work 6 days per week and 8 hours per day. Also, the employees can choose not to read or reply to the work messages after work, and their bosses cannot punish them or give them bad reviews for this. I hope this can help workers have more personal time and more rest time. At the same time, people should set clear boundaries for work. For example, after work, people can turn off work notifications and leave more time for doing exercise and having family dinners. Without such boundaries, personal life becomes the first thing to be sacrificed. In conclusion, work stress and financial pressure are closely connected to our standard of living and quality of life. However, if the government and employers provide better working conditions and individuals draw a clearer line between their jobs and the rest of their lives, this problem can be solved.', 365, 379, 19, 47, 'British English', 'Edmund Sir', 'approved', 1, false, false, 'Dataset 11 from the supplied Grammar Dataset 3 to 18 PDF. Approved for canonical storage in the development partition; excluded from live retrieval pending a separate production review. The personal source label was omitted; the canonical text contains no student identifier. The canonical 365-word source count uses the normalized one-space sentence join; the PDF metadata declares 366.'
