select '2026-08-02.1', 'PARA-0012', 'WORKPLACE_UNIFORMS_AND_CUSTOMER_TRUST_0012', 'Workplace Uniforms and Customer Trust', 'Employment / Uniform Policy / Customer Service', 'B1–B2', 'In recent years, more and more companies requires staff needed to wore uniforms at work. There are some advantages of a company having a uniform for example customer can quickly locate staff in retail stores and enhanced trust and professionalism. In staff opinion, a uniform can doesn’t required a work wardrobe expenses and it can less wear and tear on personal clothes To begin with, the advantage is that customers can easily located their staff who are wearing uniforms. Customers can have a first impression of the business. A clear illustration, if you enter an international airport with the staff do not wearing a proper uniform, you will think that there are a loss of trusts and professionalism. However, it will have more commutations with passengers and staff if they wearing uniforms. A further dimensions is you will easy to locate the staff of a shops and it will increase companies profits, imaged if you enter a retai shop and no staff wearing uniform, you will need more time to figure out someone looking at a shelf is an employees and it is no good at all.', 'In recent years, more and more companies require staff to wear uniforms at work. There are some advantages of a company having a uniform policy; for example, customers can quickly locate staff in retail stores, and uniforms enhance trust and professionalism. In the staff''s opinion, a uniform can reduce expenses for a work wardrobe and wear and tear on personal clothes. To begin with, the advantage is that customers can easily locate staff who are wearing uniforms. Customers can have a first impression of the business. As a clear illustration, if you enter an international airport where the staff are not wearing a proper uniform, you will think that there is a loss of trust and professionalism. However, there will be more communication between passengers and staff if the staff wear uniforms. A further dimension is that you will easily locate the staff in a shop, and this will increase companies'' profits; imagine entering a retail shop where no staff are wearing a uniform: you will need more time to figure out whether someone looking at a shelf is an employee, and it is no good at all.', 187, 188, 8, 38, 'British English', 'Edmund Sir', 'approved', 1, false, false, 'Dataset 12 from the supplied Grammar Dataset 3 to 18 PDF. Approved for canonical storage in the development partition; excluded from live retrieval pending a separate production review. The incomplete source punctuation in S03 is retained because it is itself an annotated development issue.'
